 Housekeeping scripts for the CI workers.
 
-`bin/clean-workspaces.sh` removes stale build workspaces under `workspaces/`. The root and
-the age threshold are hardcoded, so a worker with a different layout needs its own copy of
-the script.
+## `bin/clean-workspaces.sh`
+
+Removes stale build workspaces: each directory directly under the root whose newest file is
+more than the threshold number of days old. A workspace with no files is aged by its own
+modification time. Symlinks are never followed or removed.
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh [-n] [-r ROOT] [-d DAYS]
+```
+
+| Option | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `-r`, `--root ROOT` | `workspaces` | Directory holding the workspaces (relative paths resolve from the current directory) |
+| `-d`, `--days DAYS` | `7` | Age threshold in whole days; older workspaces are removed |
+| `-n`, `--dry-run` | off | List what would be removed (`would remove NAME (age Nd)`) and remove nothing |
+| `-h`, `--help` | | Print usage |
+
+Examples:
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh                          # workspaces/, 7 days, as before
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh -n -r /srv/ci/work -d 3  # preview on another worker
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --root /srv/ci/work --days 3
+```
+
+Exit status: `0` success, `1` a removal failed, `64` bad usage or arguments, `66` the root is
+not a directory.
